      },
      "message": "fix(motion): hold the bore exit on a coarse rim; spread the laps' kinks (held)\n\nHeld work for #1050, not ready to merge. The growth rings' disc phase\n(circles out of the entry bore, a wall conforming to the rim) is read\non the planner's rim and on a rim twice as coarse (`adaptive::conform`),\nthe worse kept; the closing laps' fillet-to-wall kinks are spread\n(`tidy::smooth_walk`). The r6.2 neck levels read 17.3 / 17.7 % D and\n0 breaks (were 20.3 % and 3); the r7 twins post no break at 5.0. The\nmeasured pins R62_LOAD_FACTOR, R62_BREAKS and BAR_50_BREAKS are removed.\n\nNot mergeable: adaptive_hsm's hsm_report_full_resolution goes red - the\nnarrow slot's changed plan posts a retract hop that rapids onto a\nsub-cell wall-side sliver (RapidInStock, 4 descents for 2 levels) the\nplanner's stock does not see. See the issue comment.\n\nRefs #1050\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
