      "message": "fix(motion): land a rapid only on stock the cut pieces swept; hold the bore exit on a coarse rim\n\n#1169: the microlift plan read its landings on the planner's cell\nbitmap, where a wall strip thinner than a cell stands unseen between\ntwo rows of cell centers. The return over the retract plane rapided to\nits lift with such a strip under the rim (narrow slot 14x60, one\nRapidInStock). The plan now keeps the segments its pieces cut\n(adaptive::lift_swept) and a rapid lands only where the whole footprint\nis proved swept - a quadtree over the disc on exact segment distances,\nrefused where the proof does not close. The hop's landing prefers a\nswept lead point; a piece starting where the tool stands is ridden on\nto at the floor instead of a retract and plunge on one spot (the slot's\ntwo extra descents).\n\n#1050: with that settled the held fix stands (16e129bb): the disc phase\nout of the bore is held on the planner's rim and a rim twice as coarse,\nthe closing laps' fillet kinks are spread at 4 degrees, and the\nmeasured pins R62_LOAD_FACTOR / R62_BREAKS / BAR_50_BREAKS are gone.\nr6.2 neck: 20.3 % D and 3 breaks -> 17.3 / 17.7 % D, 0 breaks.\n\nPinned by lift_swept::tests (sub-cell strip landing refused),\nlift_tests::a_piece_starting_where_the_tool_stands_is_ridden_on_to,\nadaptive_hsm::hsm_report_full_resolution and rotary_adaptive.\n\nFixes #1169\nFixes #1050\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
