      "message": "fix(motion): prove a landing against the cut as the verifier reads it (arc chords, 12.5 um)\n\nThe swept-stock proof held a cut 5 um off its planned chord; the\nverifier flattens a posted arc at its gouge tolerance (10 um, inside\nthe arc) on top of the 2.5 um arc fit. FIT is 12.5 um, so a landing the\nproof accepts is one the verifier's column reading accepts too.\n\nRefs #1169\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
